#version 460
// THE SCREEN-PROBE GATHER, JOB 4 OF 4: BACK TO THE PIXELS
// (GATHER-1a; the plane-weighted SH integrate PHOTON-GATHER-1b item 3,
// SPECS/photon/C2_GATHER_FILTERED_DEFAULT_ON_DESIGN.md section 1.3).
//
// ONE THREAD PER PIXEL. The pixel reads the FOUR uniform probes around it —
// bilinear in probe space, the cells whose centres bracket the pixel — plus its
// own cell's ADAPTIVE twin, and weighs each by THE PLANE TEST (the pixel's
// distance off the probe's plane as a fraction of its own view distance, and
// the two normals' dot — jahPlaneWeight, the tolerances the placement job's
// adaptive test uses, as ramps). Each probe answers with its SH EVALUATED AT
// THE PIXEL'S OWN NORMAL, so the irradiance follows the surface the pixel is
// on, not the one the probe sat on. The twin carries its cell's bilinear share.
//
// WHAT THE PLANE WEIGHT DECIDES. A cell's probes describe the surfaces they
// sit on; a pixel belongs to the ones whose plane it lies in. Weighing by
// distance to the PLANE (and by normal agreement) rather than by distance in
// pixels is what keeps a bounce on the side of a silhouette it belongs to —
// "leaks confined to the plane", the property the whole probe shape exists for.
// A pixel whose weights sum below the floor (p.knobs4.y) gets NO answer (w = 0)
// and keeps the fallback — the irradiance field's cage where one is bound
// (the fork commit for patch 0086's hook), the environment where none is.
//
// THE OUTPUT is `jahProbeIrradiance`: rgb = E/pi at the pixel's normal (what
// `envColourD` is — the trace's header), w = 1 where probes answered and 0
// where none did. A pixel gets exactly ONE diffuse-GI term in every regime.
//
// DETERMINISM: the five taps are read and summed in ONE FIXED ORDER.
//
// THE PIXEL HISTORY (PHOTON-GATHER-1c item 1; C2 design section 2). The answer
// above is one frame's estimate — 64 jittered rays a probe, a jittered probe a
// cell — and a pixel's irradiance is a quantity of its SURFACE POINT alone: the
// integrand E(x, n) = INTEGRAL L cos has no view vector in it, so the value at a
// world point does not change when the camera does. That is what makes a
// temporal mean at pixel resolution both possible and cheap: last frame's mean
// at THIS surface point is found through the previous camera
// (jah_reproject.glsl, rq_reflect.comp's arithmetic, one text), VALIDATED as
// the same surface — its stored distance within the 5 % test AND its stored
// normal within the gather's own same-surface tolerance (p.plane.y, the plane
// test's) — and blended with this frame's estimate by the COUNT kept in the
// history (a true running mean while young, then a floor so it follows a
// changing scene). NEVER A NEIGHBOURHOOD CLAMP: a clamp to this frame's local
// range is a statement that the history is WRONG wherever it disagrees with
// one noisy frame, which throws away exactly the averaging the history exists
// for; the surface tests are the only rejection.
//
// WHAT THE HISTORY HOLDS, per pixel, in two ping-ponged pairs (a pixel reads the
// mean at its reprojected coordinate while its neighbours write theirs — one
// image would make that a race):
//   radiance  rgba16f   rgb = the mean of (E/pi x coverage), a = the mean
//                       COVERAGE — PREMULTIPLIED, so a pixel a probe answers on
//                       some frames and not others (the jittered probes, a
//                       plane test at its tolerance) holds the answered frames'
//                       mean irradiance at the FRACTION of frames that answered,
//                       and hands the rest to the fallback smoothly instead of
//                       flickering between the two estimators frame by frame;
//                       and a pixel no probe answers any more fades to the
//                       fallback at the history's own rate.
//   geometry  r32ui     the surface's view distance (half), its normal
//                       (octahedral, 5 + 5 bits — the test is at 25 degrees)
//                       and the count (6 bits).
// THE BUILDER'S NOTES (C2 design, section 2): the history is in IRRADIANCE
// space at the pixel — the atlas' re-weighting (note a) is inside the unbiased
// quadrature the SH was projected with, the atlas' hit distances (note b) never
// enter it (its distance is the SURFACE's), and the SH anchor (note c) is
// evaluated before it: the history averages E/pi, never coefficients.
//
// RULE 5 (PAN-SMEAR-1), point by point. (1) A pixel new to the screen — off the
// previous picture, behind the previous camera, reprojected onto a texel that
// held no surface — restarts its mean from this frame's estimate at FULL
// weight: there is no warm-up fade anywhere in this history (the ray tier's
// eight-frame fade exists because one GGX ray is not an estimate of a lobe; a
// gather pixel's first frame is a 9-probe, 576-ray filtered estimate), so no
// band can form on the side a pan turns toward. (2) The VIEW'S AGE (p.knobs5.x)
// decides whether the previous images hold anything at all — a first frame, a
// resize, a scene bind never read them. (3) "What the ray reached": a
// reflection's history must validate what it REFLECTS because the reflected
// point moves with the eye; a diffuse pixel's hemisphere does not depend on the
// eye, so the SURFACE test is the whole validation — the one view-dependent
// input left (the camera-centred cascades that shade a hit) moves by a cascade
// step, which is exactly what a temporal mean is for (gi.gather_motion measures
// the truck and the yaw).
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require

layout( local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8, local_size_z = 1 ) in;

#define JAH_PROBE_PARAMS_BINDING 0
#include "jah_probe_params.glsl"

layout( std430, set = 0, binding = 1 ) readonly buffer Records { JahProbeRecord r[]; } records;
layout( set = 0, binding = 2 ) uniform sampler2D gBufNormals;
layout( set = 0, binding = 3 ) uniform sampler2D sceneDepth;
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 4 ) uniform image2D probeIrradiance;
/// THE PIXEL HISTORY, ping-ponged (see the header): the previous frame's pair,
/// read at the reprojected coordinate, and this frame's, written at this pixel.
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 5 ) uniform readonly image2D historyPrev;
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 6 ) uniform writeonly image2D historyCur;
layout( r32ui, set = 0, binding = 7 ) uniform readonly uimage2D historyGeomPrev;
layout( r32ui, set = 0, binding = 8 ) uniform writeonly uimage2D historyGeomCur;
/// THE REST MEAN (PHOTON-GATHER-1d): at rest — the camera, the lighting and the
/// scene held still (p.knobs6.x = the rest frame k >= 1) — a TRUE MEAN of the rest
/// frames' estimates, restarted at the first rest frame, premultiplied by
/// coverage like the history. The same pixel reads and writes it (the camera has
/// not moved, so there is no reprojection and no race): one image, not a pair.
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 9 ) uniform image2D restMean;

#include "jah_reproject.glsl"

/// The history's count saturates here (6 bits); the blend reads it only up to
/// 1 / the floor, which is far below.
const uint kHistoryCountMax = 63u;

/// THE HISTORY'S GEOMETRY WORD: the view distance as a half (its 11-bit
/// mantissa is 0.05 % — a hundred times finer than the 5 % test), the normal
/// as an octahedral pair at 5 bits each (about 3 degrees; the test is at 25),
/// and the count. Zero is "no surface here", which the distance test rejects.
vec2 octEncode( vec3 n )
{
	vec2 o = n.xy / max( abs( n.x ) + abs( n.y ) + abs( n.z ), 1e-6 );
	if( n.z < 0.0 )
		o = ( 1.0 - abs( o.yx ) ) * vec2( o.x >= 0.0 ? 1.0 : -1.0, o.y >= 0.0 ? 1.0 : -1.0 );
	return o;
}
vec3 octDecode( vec2 o )
{
	vec3 n = vec3( o, 1.0 - abs( o.x ) - abs( o.y ) );
	if( n.z < 0.0 )
		n.xy = ( 1.0 - abs( n.yx ) ) * vec2( n.x >= 0.0 ? 1.0 : -1.0, n.y >= 0.0 ? 1.0 : -1.0 );
	return normalize( n );
}
uint packGeom( float dist, vec3 n, uint count )
{
	const uint d = packHalf2x16( vec2( dist, 0.0 ) ) & 0xFFFFu;
	const uvec2 q = uvec2( clamp( round( ( octEncode( n ) * 0.5 + 0.5 ) * 31.0 ), vec2( 0.0 ),
								  vec2( 31.0 ) ) );
	return d | ( q.x << 16u ) | ( q.y << 21u ) | ( min( count, kHistoryCountMax ) << 26u );
}
void unpackGeom( uint g, out float dist, out vec3 n, out uint count )
{
	dist = unpackHalf2x16( g & 0xFFFFu ).x;
	n = octDecode( vec2( float( ( g >> 16u ) & 31u ), float( ( g >> 21u ) & 31u ) ) / 31.0 * 2.0 -
				   1.0 );
	count = g >> 26u;
}

/// E/pi of probe `i` at the unit normal n, reading only the vec4s of the SH
/// the bands need straight from the buffer (4 bands = three vec4, 9 = seven):
/// the record is 160 bytes and the integrate's memory traffic is the price the
/// SH9 record was measured at (PHOTON-GATHER-1b item 3).
vec3 shEvalAt( uint i, vec3 n, int bands )
{
	float y[9];
	jahShBasis9( n, y );
	const int vecs = bands > 4 ? 7 : 3;
	float c[28];
	for( int v = 0; v < 7; ++v )
	{
		const vec4 q = v < vecs ? records.r[i].sh[v] : vec4( 0.0 );
		c[4 * v] = q.x; c[4 * v + 1] = q.y; c[4 * v + 2] = q.z; c[4 * v + 3] = q.w;
	}
	vec3 e = vec3( 0.0 );
	for( int k = 0; k < 9; ++k )
	{
		if( k >= bands )
			break;
		e += vec3( c[3 * k], c[3 * k + 1], c[3 * k + 2] ) * y[k];
	}
	return max( e, vec3( 0.0 ) );
}

void main()
{
	const ivec2 full = ivec2( p.resolution.zw );
	const ivec2 pix = ivec2( gl_GlobalInvocationID.xy );
	if( any( greaterThanEqual( pix, full ) ) )
		return;
	const ivec2 grid = ivec2( p.resolution.xy );
	const float stride = max( p.knobs.x, 1.0 );
	const ivec2 cell = clamp( ivec2( vec2( pix ) / stride ), ivec2( 0 ), grid - 1 );
	const uint index = uint( cell.y * grid.x + cell.x );

	// The pixel's own surface, from the same prepass the probes were placed on.
	const vec2 uv = ( vec2( pix ) + 0.5 ) / vec2( full );
	const float rawDepth = texture( sceneDepth, uv ).x;
	vec3 pixelNormal = vec3( 0.0 );
	vec3 pixelWorld = vec3( 0.0 );
	float pixelDist = 0.0;
	bool pixelValid = false;
	if( rawDepth > 0.0 && rawDepth < 1.0 )
	{
		vec3 normalVS = texture( gBufNormals, uv ).xyz * 2.0 - 1.0;
		if( dot( normalVS, normalVS ) > 1e-6 )
		{
			normalVS = normalize( normalVS );
			pixelNormal = normalize( p.viewAxisX.xyz * normalVS.x + p.viewAxisY.xyz * normalVS.y +
									 p.viewAxisZ.xyz * normalVS.z );
			pixelDist = jahViewDistance( rawDepth );
			pixelWorld = jahWorldAt( uv, pixelDist );
			pixelValid = finite3( pixelWorld ) && finite3( pixelNormal ) && finite1( pixelDist );
		}
	}
	const bool temporal = p.knobs5.z > 0.5;
	if( !pixelValid )
	{
		// The sky, or a pixel the prepass never drew. No probe answers for it —
		// and nothing should: it has no hemisphere. Its history is "no surface"
		// (a zero word fails every distance test).
		imageStore( probeIrradiance, pix, vec4( 0.0 ) );
		if( temporal )
		{
			imageStore( historyCur, pix, vec4( 0.0 ) );
			imageStore( historyGeomCur, pix, uvec4( 0u ) );
			if( p.knobs6.x >= 1.0 )
				imageStore( restMean, pix, vec4( 0.0 ) );
		}
		return;
	}

	// THE FOUR GRID PROBES AROUND THE PIXEL: the cells whose centres bracket
	// it, and the bilinear weights of that bracket. A cell off the grid clamps
	// onto the border cell (its weight joins the border's).
	const vec2 g = ( vec2( pix ) + 0.5 ) / stride - 0.5;
	const ivec2 c0 = ivec2( floor( g ) );
	const vec2 f = g - vec2( c0 );
	const int bands = p.knobs4.x > 5.0 ? 9 : 4;
	const float weightFloor = max( p.knobs4.y, 1e-6 );

	vec3 sum = vec3( 0.0 );
	float wsum = 0.0;
	float ownCellWeight = 0.0;
	for( int k = 0; k < 4; ++k )
	{
		const ivec2 o = ivec2( k & 1, k >> 1 );
		const ivec2 c = clamp( c0 + o, ivec2( 0 ), grid - 1 );
		const float wb = ( o.x == 1 ? f.x : 1.0 - f.x ) * ( o.y == 1 ? f.y : 1.0 - f.y );
		if( c == cell )
			ownCellWeight += wb;
		const uint probeIndex = uint( c.y * grid.x + c.x );
		const vec4 posW = records.r[probeIndex].posW;
		if( posW.w < 0.5 || records.r[probeIndex].irradiance.w < 0.5 || wb <= 0.0 )
			continue;
		const float w = wb * jahPlaneWeight( posW.xyz, records.r[probeIndex].normalW.xyz, pixelWorld,
											 pixelNormal, pixelDist );
		if( w <= 0.0 )
			continue;
		sum += shEvalAt( probeIndex, pixelNormal, bands ) * w;
		wsum += w;
	}
	// ...AND THE PIXEL'S OWN CELL'S ADAPTIVE TWIN, at that cell's bilinear share:
	// it exists because the cell holds a surface its uniform probe is not on.
	{
		const float link = records.r[index].normalW.w;
		if( link > 0.5 && ownCellWeight > 0.0 )
		{
			const uint twin = uint( link ) - 1u;
			const vec4 posW = records.r[twin].posW;
			if( posW.w > 0.5 && records.r[twin].irradiance.w > 0.5 )
			{
				const float w = ownCellWeight * jahPlaneWeight( posW.xyz, records.r[twin].normalW.xyz,
																pixelWorld, pixelNormal, pixelDist );
				if( w > 0.0 )
				{
					sum += shEvalAt( twin, pixelNormal, bands ) * w;
					wsum += w;
				}
			}
		}
	}
	vec4 answer = vec4( 0.0 );
	if( wsum >= weightFloor )
		answer = vec4( clamp( sum / wsum, vec3( 0.0 ), vec3( 1024.0 ) ), 1.0 );
	if( !temporal )
	{
		// THE MEASUREMENT LEVER (JAHSHAKA_GATHER_NO_TEMPORAL): this frame's
		// estimate alone, and no history is read or written.
		imageStore( probeIrradiance, pix, answer );
		return;
	}

	// ---- THE PIXEL HISTORY (see the header) ---------------------------------
	vec4 prev = vec4( 0.0 );
	uint prevCount = 0u;
	if( p.knobs5.x >= 1.0 )
	{
		vec2 was;
		float z;
		if( jahReproject( pixelWorld, p.prevCamPos.xyz, p.prevCamPos.w, p.prevRayTL.xyz,
						  p.prevRayRight.xyz, p.prevRayDown.xyz, p.prevFwd.xyz, was, z ) == 0 )
		{
			const ivec2 pc = clamp( ivec2( was * vec2( full ) ), ivec2( 0 ), full - 1 );
			float wasDist;
			vec3 wasNormal;
			uint wasCount;
			unpackGeom( imageLoad( historyGeomPrev, pc ).x, wasDist, wasNormal, wasCount );
			// THE SAME SURFACE: the same distance (the 5 % test) AND the same
			// facing (the gather's own same-surface tolerance, the plane test's
			// normal dot). A corner or a crease reprojects onto a surface at the
			// same distance facing elsewhere, which the distance alone would pass.
			// (knobs5.w = 1 is the test door that turns BOTH tests off —
			// GatherTuning::historyValidationOff, the arm gi.gather_motion
			// proves its disocclusion bar against; never shipped.)
			const bool accept = p.knobs5.w > 0.5 ||
								( jahSameDistance( wasDist, z ) &&
								  dot( wasNormal, pixelNormal ) >= p.plane.y );
			if( wasCount > 0u && accept )
			{
				const vec4 h = imageLoad( historyPrev, pc );
				if( finite3( h.xyz ) && finite1( h.w ) )
				{
					prev = clamp( h, vec4( 0.0 ), vec4( 1024.0, 1024.0, 1024.0, 1.0 ) );
					prevCount = wasCount;
				}
			}
		}
	}
	// THE COUNT-IN-HISTORY IDIOM (rq_reflect.comp): 1/n while the mean is young
	// — a true running mean, the fastest unbiased convergence — with a floor so
	// it keeps following a scene that changes. A pixel with no usable history
	// (count 0) takes this frame's estimate whole.
	const float floorBlend = clamp( p.knobs5.y, 1.0 / float( kHistoryCountMax ), 1.0 );
	const float blend = prevCount > 0u ? max( 1.0 / ( float( prevCount ) + 1.0 ), floorBlend )
									   : 1.0;
	vec4 mean = mix( prev, vec4( answer.xyz * answer.w, answer.w ), blend );
	// ---- AT REST, THE REST MEAN (PHOTON-GATHER-1d) ------------------------------
	// The history above is an EMA past its tenth frame, and an EMA never stops:
	// its state is a function of EVERY frame it has seen, so two pictures of one
	// still scene — a screenshot after a long settle and one after a short one —
	// differ, and a still view flickers by the floor's share of each frame's
	// noise forever. At rest the answer becomes a true mean of the rest frames
	// alone (restarted at the first, weight 1/k at the k-th: the sample sequence
	// is the rest frame's own index, so the mean is a function of the scene and
	// the camera and of nothing that happened before), handed over from the EMA
	// linearly over N frames (p.knobs6.y, the settle; no pop when a camera
	// stops), and at k = N the answer IS that mean — after which the host holds
	// the frame and dispatches nothing (OgreScreenProbeGather.cpp): a still view
	// costs the gather nothing. THE HISTORY IS WRITTEN WITH THE HANDED-OVER
	// VALUE, so when the camera moves again the EMA continues from the rest mean
	// and not from the older EMA state it would otherwise pop back to.
	const float restK = p.knobs6.x;
	if( restK >= 1.0 )
	{
		const vec4 sample1 = vec4( answer.xyz * answer.w, answer.w );
		const vec4 rest = restK < 1.5 ? sample1
									  : mix( imageLoad( restMean, pix ), sample1, 1.0 / restK );
		imageStore( restMean, pix, rest );
		mean = mix( mean, rest, clamp( restK / max( p.knobs6.y, 1.0 ), 0.0, 1.0 ) );
	}
	imageStore( historyCur, pix, mean );
	imageStore( historyGeomCur, pix, uvec4( packGeom( pixelDist, pixelNormal, prevCount + 1u ) ) );
	// The pixel's answer: the answered frames' mean irradiance at the fraction
	// of frames that answered (the piece and the field's cage are both linear in
	// the coverage, so a fraction hands that share to the fallback).
	vec4 outV = vec4( 0.0 );
	if( mean.w > 1e-3 )
		outV = vec4( clamp( mean.xyz / mean.w, vec3( 0.0 ), vec3( 1024.0 ) ), mean.w );
	imageStore( probeIrradiance, pix, outV );
}
